    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22497" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inconfūsus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>unconfused</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut inconfusus eat (mundus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 2, 45</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">recursus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. VI. Cons. Hon. 622</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>unembarrassed</i>,
				<i>not disconcerted</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animus intrepidus inconfususque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 3 praef.</span></i>
			
			<i>fin.</i>; id. de Ira, 1, 12, 3.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
